# about:themes — the reader's themes and the two stores, inside the window:
# the themes they have, to put on; Firefox's, read from the add-ons site's
# catalogue (here a file of its shape stands in for it: a script never asks
# the network), each with a "Put on" that is a plain link to the theme's
# file; and a box for a Chrome Web Store theme's address. One click puts a
# theme on: the page stays where it is, no file is saved, and the list of the
# reader's themes has the new one, in use.
resize 1000 700
themes-folder
themes-gallery ../fixtures/themes/amo-search.json
open about:themes
assert-title Themes
assert-text Yours
assert-text Solarized Dark
assert-text Sample Fox
assert-text by A Fox
assert-text 1,234,567 users
# A stranger's name is words, whatever it is made of; an entry with no file
# to put on is left out.
assert-text Chrome <b>d'essai</b>
assert-no-text No file to it
assert-text Page 1 of 3
assert-theme Sashfold

# The first card's "Put on".
click 100 540
assert-url about:themes
assert-theme Sample Fox
assert-pixel 759 0 #203040
assert-text Theme put on: Sample Fox
assert-tabs 1

# One of the reader's own, put on from the list: the second of them.
open about:themes?use=1
assert-theme Nord
assert-text Put on: Nord

# What is no Chrome Web Store address is said to be none, and nothing is fetched.
open about:themes?crx=hello+there
assert-text That is no Chrome Web Store address or id
assert-theme Nord

# A catalogue that cannot be read: the page says so, and the reader's own
# themes are there all the same.
themes-gallery ../fixtures/themes/not-a-theme.zip
open about:themes
assert-text The gallery could not be read
assert-text Solarized Dark

# The window's menu leads here — to the tab that has it, when one does.
new-tab
main-menu
menu Themes
assert-menu High Contrast | *Nord | Sashfold | Sashfold Light | Solarized Dark | Sample Fox | - | More themes…
menu More themes…
assert-url about:themes
assert-tabs 2
